Sītā trusts false head and bow and curses Kaikēyī --- Sītā collapses and revives to lament over the head --- Sītā mourns Kausalyā and lost rites and marriage vows --- Sītā begs Rāvaṇa to lay her upon Rāma --- A guard summons Rāvaṇa to urgent counsel with Prahasta --- Rāvaṇa leaves the grove and the illusion vanishes --- Rāvaṇa orders his generals to muster the army by drums